Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns & their usage  
• `starttime`: filter to 2018, derive day‑of‑week (`EXTRACT(DAYOFWEEK…)`) and hour (`EXTRACT(HOUR…)`).  
• `start_station_id`: group trips by station to find the busiest origin in 2018.  
• `start_station_name`: optional human‑readable station name.  

Typical conditions you will see in the queries  
• `EXTRACT(YEAR FROM starttime)=2018` – keep only 2018 rides.  
• `start_station_id IS NOT NULL` – ignore records without a station id.  
• `start_station_id = <most‑popular‑id>` – look only at the busiest station once it is known.  

Below are ten exploratory BigQuery SQL statements (each returns at most 20 rows) that move step‑by‑step from basic inspection to the final answer.

```sql
-- 1. Distinct ride years present in the trips table
SELECT DISTINCT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `starttime`) AS ride_year
FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york_citibike.citibike_trips`
WHERE `starttime` IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Peek at a few 2018 trips: start time & station columns
SELECT `starttime`,
       `start_station_id`,
       `start_station_name`
FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york_citibike.citibike_trips`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `starttime`)=2018
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Distinct station ids that had any trips starting in 2018
SELECT DISTINCT `start_station_id`
FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york_citibike.citibike_trips`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `starttime`)=2018
  AND `start_station_id` IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Count of 2018 trips by start station (top 20)
SELECT `start_station_id`,
       `start_station_name`,
       COUNT(*) AS trip_cnt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york_citibike.citibike_trips`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `starttime`)=2018
  AND `start_station_id` IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY `start_station_id`, `start_station_name`
ORDER BY trip_cnt DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Verify the busiest station’s monthly volume trend
SELECT EXTRACT(MONTH FROM `starttime`) AS month_num,
       COUNT(*) AS trips_in_month
FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york_citibike.citibike_trips`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `starttime`)=2018
  AND `start_station_id` = <MOST_POPULAR_ID>
GROUP BY month_num
ORDER BY month_num
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Distinct numeric day‑of‑week values (1=Sunday … 7=Saturday)
SELECT DISTINCT EXTRACT(DAYOFWEEK FROM `starttime`) AS dow_num
FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york_citibike.citibike_trips`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `starttime`)=2018
  AND `start_station_id` = <MOST_POPULAR_ID>
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Trip counts by day‑of‑week for the busiest station
SELECT EXTRACT(DAYOFWEEK FROM `starttime`) AS dow_num,
       COUNT(*) AS trips
FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york_citibike.citibike_trips`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `starttime`)=2018
  AND `start_station_id` = <MOST_POPULAR_ID>
GROUP BY dow_num
ORDER BY trips DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Trip counts by hour of day for the busiest station
SELECT EXTRACT(HOUR FROM `starttime`) AS hour_of_day,
       COUNT(*) AS trips
FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york_citibike.citibike_trips`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `starttime`)=2018
  AND `start_station_id` = <MOST_POPULAR_ID>
GROUP BY hour_of_day
ORDER BY trips DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Combined day‑of‑week & hour grid – which combo has most rides?
SELECT EXTRACT(DAYOFWEEK FROM `starttime`) AS dow_num,
       EXTRACT(HOUR FROM `starttime`)      AS hour_of_day,
       COUNT(*)                            AS trips
FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york_citibike.citibike_trips`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `starttime`)=2018
  AND `start_station_id` = <MOST_POPULAR_ID>
GROUP BY dow_num, hour_of_day
ORDER BY trips DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final: day‑of‑week & hour with the single largest 2018 trip count
SELECT EXTRACT(DAYOFWEEK FROM `starttime`) AS busiest_dow_num,
       EXTRACT(HOUR FROM `starttime`)      AS busiest_hour,
       COUNT(*)                            AS trip_total
FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york_citibike.citibike_trips`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `starttime`)=2018
  AND `start_station_id` = (
        SELECT `start_station_id`
        FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york_citibike.citibike_trips`
        WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `starttime`)=2018
          AND `start_station_id` IS NOT NULL
        GROUP BY `start_station_id`
        ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC
        LIMIT 1
      )
GROUP BY busiest_dow_num, busiest_hour
ORDER BY trip_total DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

Replace `<MOST_POPULAR_ID>` in queries 5‑9 with the station id that query 4 shows at the top.  
Running query 10 will reveal the numeric day‑of‑week and the hour of day that together had the greatest number of 2018 departures for that station.
